{marker topic}
{helpb nwtopical##programming:[NW-2.9] Programming}

{title:Title}

{p2colset 9 20 22 2}{...}
{p2col :nwvalidvars {hline 2}}Validate Stata variables for a network{p_end}
{p2colreset}{...}


{title:Syntax}

{p 8 17 2}
{cmdab: nwvalidvars} 
{it:{help int:nodes}} ,
{opth stub(string)}

{synoptline}
{p2colreset}{...}


{title:Description}

{pstd}
Validates names of Stata variables that can be used to represent a network of size {it:nodes}. Stata variables 
are generated by combining {bf:stub()} with a consecutive number. If these Stata variables already exists, the 
command comes up with a new suggestion for naming variables. This command is mostly used for progamming.


{title:Network types}

{pstd}
The command works the same for every network type (see {help nwnetworktypes}).{p_end}


{title:Limits}

{pstd}
One name per node goes into a Stata macro. When the {it:nodes} names do not fit into a macro (about 20,000 names in Stata/BE) the command stops at once with r(900) and a message.


{title:Examples}

	{cmd:. nwclear}
	{cmd:. nwwebuse gang}
	{cmd:. nwvalidvars 10, stub(g)}
	{cmd:. return list}


{title:Stored results}

{synoptset 20 tabbed}{...}
{synopt:{bf:r(stub)}}stub used to generate Stata variable names{p_end}
{synopt:{bf:r(valid)}}"true" when Stata variables do not already exist, "false" otherwise{p_end}
{synopt:{bf:r(validvars)}}list of valid Stata variables{p_end}


{title:Also see}

   {help nwvalidate}, {help nwload}

